%% title: From the syllabus to study plans
%% desc: A class and subject's syllabus holds the topics. Each subject of each section gets one study plan, with its lessons in order. The published routine gives each lesson an expected date. When the teacher reports periods, progress goes up; when they do not, the plan shows as behind.
flowchart LR
  T["Syllabus topics<br/>class + subject"]:::teacher --> P["Study plan<br/>section + subject + term"]:::teacher
  L["Template<br/>library"]:::admin -. copy .-> P
  P --> D["Expected lesson<br/>dates"]:::note
  R["Published<br/>routine"]:::admin --> D
  D --> G["Teacher reports<br/>periods"]:::teacher
  G --> S["Progress or<br/>behind"]:::note
  classDef teacher fill:#e7f5ff,stroke:#1c7ed6,color:#0b3d66
  classDef admin fill:#fff4e6,stroke:#e8590c,color:#7a2e05
  classDef guardian fill:#ebfbee,stroke:#2b8a3e,color:#14411d
  classDef note fill:#f1f3f5,stroke:#868e96,color:#343a40
